# Module-Aware Constant Table Acceptance

schema_version: 1
directive: `INBOX-31`
target: `x86_64-linux-gnu`
validation_tier: 3
result: pass

The selector and ELF writer now consume one shared typed constant-table
decoder through a read-only module context. Admission is limited to four
captured shapes: `[128 x i16]`, `[16 x double]`, `[512 x double]` with an
even 0..510 index proof, and `[128 x T]` where named `T` resolves exactly to
`{ double, double }`. The existing value-location map owns table pointers;
index normalization and stride arithmetic stay in GPRs, and symbol addresses
use the existing RIP-relative `R_X86_64_PC32` relocation path.

Focused fail-closed coverage rejects writable tables and unproved indexes.
Other layouts, pointer-bearing initializers, table stores, `.rodata`
migration, STB_LOCAL ordering, and shared-library PIC remain excluded. The
current ELF policy deliberately serializes the admitted constants as global
objects in the existing `.data` section.

A generated canary uses initializer text copied from all four captured table
shapes. Six emitted probe functions cover the i16 table, the 16-double table,
both low/high accesses to the 512-double table, and both fields of the named
pair table. A native `zig build-exe -fno-lld` link passes 18/18 precomputed
first/interior/last calls, including distinct offset-zero and offset-eight
pair loads.

`readelf` proves four defined `.data` objects at exact sizes 256, 128, 4096,
and 2048 bytes and six `.rela.text` entries. Every entry is
`R_X86_64_PC32` with addend `-4`; no new relocation kind or linker ownership
was introduced.

Fresh report-all remains 443 selected / 214 emitting / 229 failing. All six
directed rows advance past their table GEP/load frontier, but none closes:

- `compiler_rt.sqrt.sqrt` and `compiler_rt.sqrt.sqrtf` stop at
  `composed-block-mul64-rhs`;
- `compiler_rt.log.log` and `compiler_rt.exp2.__exp2h` stop at
  `composed-block-binary-width`;
- `compiler_rt.exp2.exp2` stops at `composed-block-icmp-form`;
- `compiler_rt.exp2.exp2f` stops at `composed-block-binary-width`.

Tier 2 passes all 24 build steps and 925/925 tests. The single Tier 3
invocation passes all 17 subgates and is recorded in
`docs/evidence/distribution_all_after_inbox31_constant_tables.summary`.

